{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY HITS ---\\\\n' && rg -n -i -C 1 'P58|mixed-uhf|Aristotle closeout|two-lane' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md || true && printf '\\\\n--- STATUS ---\\\\n' && git status --short && printf '\\\\n--- ROOT FILES ---\\\\n' && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'PLAN.md' -g 'TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md' -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*STATUS*' -g 'P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.md' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY HITS ---\\\\n' && rg -n -i -C 1 'P58|mixed-uhf|Aristotle closeout|two-lane' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md || true && printf '\\\\n--- STATUS ---\\\\n' && git status --short && printf '\\\\n--- ROOT FILES ---\\\\n' && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'PLAN.md' -g 'TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md' -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*STATUS*' -g 'P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.md' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n\n--- MEMORY HITS ---\n41-\n42:# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n43-\n44:scope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\n45-applies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse only after checking the live queues, `state.json`, systemd unit, Lean checkout, and Aristotle task state; no acceptance or advancement is implied by this partial rollout\n--\n50-\n51:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n52-\n\n--- STATUS ---\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n\n--- ROOT FILES ---\nAGENTS.md\nPLAN.md\naristotle_tasks/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.md\nwork/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && printf '\\\\n--- PLAN P58 CONTEXT ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 6 'P58|P5[3-9]|Lane H|mixed-UHF|Mixed' PLAN.md && printf '\\\\n--- DECISION ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.md && printf '\\\\n--- HANDOFF/STATUS FILES ---\\\\n' && rg --files work reviews | rg -i '(handoff|status|p5[3-8]|closeout|audit)' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && printf '\\\\n--- PLAN P58 CONTEXT ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 6 'P58|P5[3-9]|Lane H|mixed-UHF|Mixed' PLAN.md && printf '\\\\n--- DECISION ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.md && printf '\\\\n--- HANDOFF/STATUS FILES ---\\\\n' && rg --files work reviews | rg -i '(handoff|status|p5[3-8]|closeout|audit)' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n\n--- PLAN P58 CONTEXT ---\n21-This lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\n22-trace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\n23-separate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\n24-of a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\n25-merely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n26-\n27:### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n28-\n29-**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n30-\n31-From a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\n32-their coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\n33-models, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\n--\n39-trivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\n40-not follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\n41-spatial factorization.\n42-\n43-### Reconnection\n44-\n45:Lane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\n46-concrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\n47-the general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\n48-that the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\n49-the two results remain logically independent.\n50-\n51-## Aristotle package sequence\n--\n65-\n66-### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n67-\n68-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n69-|---|---|---|\n70-| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n71:| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n72:| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n73:| P55 | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Construct source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras and extend the P53 alpha by density. |\n74:| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Prove the stabilizer/product-state equality on finite Pauli words and extend it by density and continuity. |\n75:| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n76:| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n77:| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n78-\n79-### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n80-\n81-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n82-|---|---|---|\n83-| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Optional globalization of a full finite corner to a faithful normal semifinite weight, if needed beyond no-type-III exclusion. |\n84-| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n85-\n86-## Initial parallel wave\n87-\n88-Submit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\n89:and P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\n90-packets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\n91-they are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n92-\n93-## Non-negotiable gates\n94-\n95-1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n\n--- DECISION ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\n--- PACKET ---\n# P58 — mixed UHF factor classification\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1945-1967`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P58`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P54`, integrated and locally audited before submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed\n  hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under explicit project-local definitions.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no regional alpha transport, no pure-sector\n  classification, no spatial product factorhood, and no final trace/weight theorem.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean`. For the mixed\ncoordinates in the P54 dyadic representation, prove the finite case is a matrix\nfactor with normalized trace. For an infinite mixed subsystem, construct the\nincreasing matrix approximation and the strongest checked factor/finite-trace\nstatement available; state any analytic factoriality or hyperfinite-II1\nclassification bridge as an explicit conditional interface rather than a label\nmistaken for a proof.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList every weak closure, factoriality, normality, faithfulness, or classification\npremise explicitly.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean`; import P54 and\nthe existing dyadic trace and bicommutant modules.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor` succeeds without\nforbidden declarations. The response distinguishes matrix approximation,\nfactorhood, hyperfiniteness, and II1 classification.\n\n--- HANDOFF/STATUS FILES ---\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md\nreviews/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P39-state-preserving-gns-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P40-bicommutant-normal-transport-closeout.md\nreviews/P41-product-factor-classification-boundary-closeout.md\nreviews/P47-center-finite-projection-core-closeout.md\nreviews/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower-closeout.md\nreviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\nreviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\nreviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\nreviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md\nreviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\nreviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- ARISTOTLE REFERENCE ---' && sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PLAN GATES ---' && sed -n '90,190p' PLAN.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P54 CLOSEOUT ---' && sed -n '1,320p' reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P53 CLOSEOUT (QUEUE STATE) ---' && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- LOG ---' && tail -n 100 history/logs/20260807T121052Z-ac6dc5ea-tasks.log && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- QUARANTINE/RESPONSE DIRS ---' && find . -maxdepth 3 -type d \\\\( -iname '*response*' -o -iname '*quarantine*' -o -iname '*aristotle*' \\\\) -print | sort\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- ARISTOTLE REFERENCE ---' && sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PLAN GATES ---' && sed -n '90,190p' PLAN.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P54 CLOSEOUT ---' && sed -n '1,320p' reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P53 CLOSEOUT (QUEUE STATE) ---' && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- LOG ---' && tail -n 100 history/logs/20260807T121052Z-ac6dc5ea-tasks.log && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- QUARANTINE/RESPONSE DIRS ---' && find . -maxdepth 3 -type d \\\\( -iname '*response*' -o -iname '*quarantine*' -o -iname '*aristotle*' \\\\) -print | sort\"","aggregated_output":"--- ARISTOTLE REFERENCE ---\n# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n--- PLAN GATES ---\npackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\nthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n\n## Non-negotiable gates\n\n1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   theorem alone.\n3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n\n---\n\n# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n## Objective\n\nFormalize, from the manuscript's actual finite-support adapted-coordinate data,\na state-preserving C-star isomorphism from the quasi-local Pauli algebra to the\nregional algebra.  Obtain the represented von Neumann algebra equivalence by\nthe canonical GNS unitary, then apply an independently established product\nfactor classification.\n\nThe source basis is exclusively `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md` and the cited manuscript\nlocators.  In particular, no gLU/refinement/layer-coherence premise is allowed\nunless later added explicitly as a new auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Current position\n\nThe project already has checked conditional interfaces for:\n\n1. finite Pauli/stabilizer coordinates and pure/mixed states;\n2. algebraic direct limits, their induced algebraic equivalence `alpha`, and\n   compatible state transport;\n3. supplied C-star completions and a supplied C-star extension of `alpha`;\n4. GNS transport for supplied compatible C-star states; and\n5. supplied normal/product-factor transport.\n\nThese are scaffolding.  They do not discharge the manuscript-specific finite\ncoordinate construction or the product-factor classification.\n\n## Phase A — exact finite coordinate theorem\n\n**Goal:** Replace abstract finite-stage star equivalences by maps constructed\nfrom a finite restriction of the adapted symplectic basis.\n\n1. Specify a finite region/exhaustion and the finite Pauli label spaces.\n2. Define the coordinate map from the adapted `z_i,x_i` data.\n3. Prove the Pauli multiplier and star equations, including the required phase\n   correction.\n4. Prove the map is a finite-stage complex star-algebra equivalence.\n5. Prove its stabilizer membership criterion and the finite product-state\n   expectation formula.\n\n**Gate A:** no supplied finite-stage star equivalence remains in the finite\nmanuscript theorem; only explicitly stated finite adapted-coordinate data does.\n\n## Phase B — coherence and quasi-local C-star isomorphism\n\n**Goal:** Construct the actual C-star isomorphism `alpha`, rather than assume\nan algebraic or completed extension.\n\n1. Prove the Phase-A maps commute exactly with all finite-region inclusions.\n2. Form the algebraic direct-limit star equivalence.\n3. Specify the quasi-local C-star completions as inductive-limit completions.\n4. Prove the algebraic map is isometric on the dense quasi-local subalgebras.\n5. Extend it uniquely to a C-star star-algebra equivalence\n   `alpha : P_quasilocal ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A_regional`.\n\n**Gate B:** P23 and P25 are instantiated by proved data, not used as supplied\ninterfaces.\n\n## Phase C — state identity and GNS transport\n\n**Goal:** Prove the regional state pulled back by `alpha` is the pure/mixed\nproduct state.\n\n1. Check equality on finite Pauli-word bases using Phase A's stabilizer\ncriterion.\n2. Prove compatibility under inclusions and hence equality on the quasi-local\nC-star algebra by density/continuity.\n3. Instantiate the existing C-star/GNS bridge to obtain the canonical GNS\nunitary and its intertwining identity.\n4. Use conjugation by that unitary to identify the represented von Neumann\nalgebras.\n\n**Gate C:** do not use a separate quasi-equivalence/normal-folium argument.\nIt is unnecessary once the state-preserving C-star isomorphism is proved.\n\n## Phase D — product representation classification\n\n**Goal:** Independently prove or source the product-state representation\ntheorem.\n--- P54 CLOSEOUT ---\n# P54 closeout review — faithful UHF reference representation\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P54-uhf-reference-representation.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`2843359fff4021ff2350373fd8ec82c3ffd0948ccf723193b5bc996a0d084668`) and\nextracted, without building, updating, or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9` in both\nlocations.  The archive and extraction remain raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module imports only the pre-existing, byte-identical live modules\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`,\n`AristotleCandidates.AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation`, and\n`AristotleCandidates.ConcreteCStarCompletion`.\n\nIt constructs the following principal declarations:\n\n- `UHFL2`, `uhfL2Core`, and `UHFGNS`, the trace-GNS pre-Hilbert space of\n  `QubitUHFAlgebra` and its `UniformSpace.Completion`;\n- `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`, `qubitUHF_exists_bound`,\n  `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`, and `uhfNormSq_mul_le`;\n- `uhfRep : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)`, together with\n  `uhfRep_injective`, `uhfCyclicVector_norm`, and\n  `uhfRep_vector_state`;\n- the compatible finite-stage family `uhfStageRep` and\n  `uhfRepData : QubitOperatorRepresentationData UHFGNS`, with\n  `uhfStageRep_compat`, `uhfRepData_rho_injective`,\n  `uhfRepData_limitRep`, and `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`; and\n- the concrete closed operator-range C-star algebra `UHFConcreteCStar` with\n  its injective dense embedding `uhfConcreteEmbedding` and\n  `uhfConcreteEmbedding_denseRange`.\n\nThere are **no supplied auxiliary assumptions**: boundedness is established\nfrom the internal algebraic sum-of-squares cone `sumSqCone` and the finite\ndyadic matrix tower; faithfulness comes from the constructed canonical trace.\nThe Hilbert space is a completion of that pre-Hilbert space, not an assumed\ninfinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The module constructs a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the algebraic dyadic limit, including injective finite-stage representations and the induced-limit identification. |\n| partial | The concrete closure is an operator-range C-star model, but P54 deliberately does not identify it with a project-specific regional completion or prove a spatial tensor-product model. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the P54 gate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope.  The additional\nclosed operator-range C-star construction is supporting infrastructure and\ndoes not weaken or replace the requested faithful reference representation.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P54, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** none.  The packet is one of the four explicitly approved\n  independent foundation packages.  Its three imports are prior local\n  infrastructure, not P47--P61 dependencies, and were byte-identical in the\n  quarantine snapshot and live checkout.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator\n  representation of the dyadic algebraic limit is constructed from finite\n  stages, without assuming an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The candidate neither defines\n  a regional alpha nor proves a state identity for a regional algebra, a\n  spatial tensor product, factorhood/type, or a trace/weight classification.\n  Its trace-GNS vector-state identity concerns only the constructed dyadic\n  reference representation and is not such a classification claim.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation` — passed in\n  the live project.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation Formalization`\n  — passed in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` —\n  passed.  Because the new untracked module was not emitted as an `.olean` by\n  the package target, the same live source was explicitly compiled with\n  `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.olean ...`\n  before importing it for the axiom report.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`, `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`,\n  `uhfNormSq_mul_le`, `uhfRep`, `uhfRep_injective`, `uhfStageRep_compat`,\n  `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`, and `uhfConcreteEmbedding_denseRange` —\n  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and direct imports — no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide` occurrence.  Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and\n  `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the completion is\nexplicitly the trace-GNS completion rather than an infinite tensor product;\nthat the bounded left action is proved from the algebraic cone bound rather\nthan supplied as a completion/isometry interface; that the finite-stage\ncompatibility and limit faithfulness are actual declarations; and that the\ncandidate does not cross into P55--P59 regional, spatial, factor, or\ntrace/weight claims.  Lean compilation and axiom reports validate this\nformal infrastructure only; they do not establish any manuscript statement\nor later analytic tensor-factor conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P54 candidate, the raw quarantine archive\nand extraction, this closeout review, and the generated live `.olean` cache\nunder the existing `.lake/build/` tree.  All pre-existing modified and\nuntracked work was preserved.  No manuscript file was changed; no commit,\npush, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n--- P53 CLOSEOUT (QUEUE STATE) ---\n# P53 closeout review — local-hyperbolic algebraic alpha\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project for task\n`11e84c2b-b0a0-420f-ac80-d38a8a5695bb` was downloaded to\n`aristotle_responses/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256\n`89df64accdc83453c13fe7a5a9c6080b80811a3df44947576b0d9e342a100a4f`)\nand extracted, without a build, update, or dependency fetch, under\n`aristotle_responses/P53-quarantine/`. Only the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` was integrated into\nthe live project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n`797dd652c0cef03fd6481aee5331446fdad4dba7f4db9f310bda6d6b76efcd1b`.\nThe archive, extraction, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` remain raw response\nrecords; no other candidate module was copied.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module defines the concrete finite twisted-Pauli-word algebra\n`pauliAlgebra`, its word basis `pauliWordBasis`, the coordinate pairing\n`coordPairing`, and `AlphaData`. Under `AlphaData A`, the load-bearing\ndeclarations are:\n\n- `stageLabelMap_bijective`: every finite-stage label map is a bijection;\n- `stage_mulCompatible` and `stage_starCompatible`: the explicitly defined\n  quadratic phase satisfies the word multiplication and involution equations;\n- `stage`: a constructed `FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, with no supplied\n  finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv` field;\n- `directedFamily`: the coherent finite-stage system;\n- `alpha`: the resulting algebraic direct-limit `StarAlgEquiv`;\n- `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`, `alpha_symm_word`, and\n  `existsUnique_alpha`: the phase-calibrated word and inverse formulas and\n  uniqueness; and\n- `standardAlphaData`: a tautological non-vacuity witness on `Nat`.\n\nThe conditional premises are explicit fields of `AlphaData`:\n\n1. P52's `LocalHyperbolicFamily.indep` and `LatticeExhaustion` data;\n2. `[LinearOrder I]`, used solely for the quadratic-phase ordering convention;\n3. `symplectic`, equality of the antisymmetrized source and target Pauli\n   pairings; and\n4. `stage_surjective`, onto-ness of each finite source-label block onto its\n   regional target-label block.\n\nP52 already proves injectivity and inclusion coherence. P53 derives stage\nbijectivity by combining that proof with `stage_surjective`; it does not hide\nstage equivalences, phase calibration, or whole-stage coherence in fields.\nThe local `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` conditions are additional\nauxiliary assumptions, not consequences established from the manuscript in\nthis repository.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From the named P52 data plus `symplectic` and `stage_surjective`, P53 constructs the finite twisted Pauli algebras, phase-calibrated finite-stage star equivalences, commuting directed system, and algebraic direct-limit star equivalence `alpha`. |\n| partial | The manuscript specialization is conditional: the repository does not construct the actual regional symplectic-coordinate realization or prove the stage-surjectivity premise from the cited manuscript clauses. The formula on generators is phase-calibrated, not an unphased literal equality. |\n| blocked | No obstruction blocks this algebraic gate. The next gates—concrete C-star realization/extension, product-state identity, GNS spatial tensor splitting, factorhood, and trace/weight classification—remain P54--P59 work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated conditional scope. The\nalternative route builds a project-local finite twisted-word algebra rather\nthan assuming stage equivalences. This adds precisely `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective` as premises; it does not weaken the requested conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P53, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** P52 is integrated, compiled, and locally audited in\n  `reviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md`. The module\n  imports P52 plus checked phase/coherence/direct-limit infrastructure; it\n  imports no later P54--P61 package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed phase-calibrated finite-stage\n  star equivalences, their coherent algebraic direct-limit equivalence, and\n  the direct-limit `alpha` word formulas.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The module explicitly makes no\n  C-star completion, state identity, GNS tensor split, spatial tensor-product,\n  factorhood, trace, or weight theorem, and no such declaration occurs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` — passed\n  in the live project (8045 jobs); no build ran in quarantine.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `stageLabelMap_bijective`, `stage_mulCompatible`, `stage_starCompatible`,\n  `directedFamily`, `alpha`, `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`,\n  `existsUnique_alpha`, and `standardAlphaData` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan across the candidate and its direct P52/phase/direct-limit\n  imports — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that finite-stage\nsurjectivity is exposed rather than inferred from P52, that symmetry of the\ndiscrepancy is obtained only from the named symplectic premise, that the\nquadratic phase is used in both multiplication and star compatibility, and\nthat `alpha_zWord`/`alpha_xWord` retain the phase. Compilation validates the\nformal conditional construction; it does not establish the manuscript's\ngeometric realization or any later analytic/operator-algebraic statement.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P53 candidate, its response archive,\nquarantine extraction, and this review. Pre-existing untracked P49/P49A/P49B\ncandidate and review files remain untouched. No manuscript file was changed;\nno commit, push, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was\nperformed.\n--- LOG ---\nID                                   CREATED              NAME                           STATUS         \n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ned55ef94-0313-4123-9cc0-b00ffdb465aa 1 hour ago           # Autonomous proof-developm... COMPLETE       \n--- QUARANTINE/RESPONSE DIRS ---\n./AristotleCandidates\n./aristotle_responses\n./aristotle_responses/P37-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-y537ze25_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P39-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-oadr2kun_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P40-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-hpzu5w6c_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P41-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-7viao_05_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P47-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p47-80u8nxnx_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P48-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p48-48zqafp9_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P49-quarantine\n./aristotle_responses/P49-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49-gizp5x2z_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P49A-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49a-p0kpdbli_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P49B-quarantine\n./aristotle_responses/P49B-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49b-sn5_fvfw_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P52-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p52-mmt9py1p_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P53-quarantine\n./aristotle_responses/P53-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p53-6si5fpxx_aristotle\n./aristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle\n./aristotle_tasks\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
