{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"task_root='aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- CANDIDATE REMAINDER ---'\nsed -n '421,1100p' \\\"\"'$task_root/AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- P49B CLOSEOUT ---'\nsed -n '1,360p' reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- P49A CLOSEOUT ---'\nsed -n '1,180p' reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- DIRECT IMPORT HASH COMPARISON ---'\nfor f in Formalization/DyadicTensorTower.lean AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean AristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean; do sha256sum \\\"\"'$f\" \"$task_root/$f\"; done\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- SOURCE CONTRACT LOCATOR ---'\nrg -n -C 4 '1945|1967|mixed|hyperfinite|II' SOURCE-CONTRACT.md\"","aggregated_output":"--- CANDIDATE REMAINDER ---\n\n/-! ## 5. Matrix representations generate factors: an unconditional theorem -/\n\nsection MatrixFactor\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-- **Project-local definition (factor).**  A concrete von Neumann algebra is a\n*factor* when its centre consists of the scalar operators. -/\ndef HasTrivialOperatorCenter (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : Prop :=\n  ∀ x ∈ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)),\n    (∀ y ∈ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), y * x = x * y) → ∃ c : ℂ, x = c • 1\n\n/-- The rank-one operator `w ↦ ⟪v, w⟫ • u`. -/\nnoncomputable def rankOneOp (u v : H) : H →L[ℂ] H := (innerSL ℂ v).smulRight u\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n@[simp] theorem rankOneOp_apply (u v w : H) : rankOneOp u v w = ⟪v, w⟫_ℂ • u := rfl\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n/-- **Corner scalars.**  If `p` is a nonzero idempotent operator and `y = p y p`\ncommutes with every operator of the corner `p B(H) p`, then `y` is a scalar\nmultiple of `p`. -/\ntheorem corner_commutant_eq_scalar {p y : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : p * p = p) (hp0 : p ≠ 0)\n    (hy : y = p * y * p) (hcomm : ∀ T : H →L[ℂ] H, y * (p * T * p) = (p * T * p) * y) :\n    ∃ c : ℂ, y = c • p := by\n  have hpy : p * y = y := by\n    conv_lhs => rw [hy]\n    rw [← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, hp]\n    exact hy.symm\n  have hyp : y * p = y := by\n    conv_lhs => rw [hy]\n    rw [mul_assoc, hp]\n    exact hy.symm\n  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ : ∃ v : H, p v ≠ 0 := by\n    by_contra hcon\n    push_neg at hcon\n    exact hp0 (by ext w; simp [hcon w])\n  set v0 : H := p v with hv0\n  have hpv0 : p v0 = v0 := by\n    have h := congrArg (fun T : H →L[ℂ] H => T v) hp\n    simpa [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, hv0] using h\n  have hinner : ⟪v0, v0⟫_ℂ ≠ 0 := inner_self_ne_zero.mpr hv\n  refine ⟨⟪v0, y v0⟫_ℂ / ⟪v0, v0⟫_ℂ, ?_⟩\n  have key : ∀ u : H, y (p u) = (⟪v0, y v0⟫_ℂ / ⟪v0, v0⟫_ℂ) • p u := by\n    intro u\n    have h := congrArg (fun T : H →L[ℂ] H => T v0) (hcomm (rankOneOp u v0))\n    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, rankOneOp_apply] at h\n    rw [hpv0] at h\n    have hpyv0 : p (y v0) = y v0 := by\n      have hh := congrArg (fun T : H →L[ℂ] H => T v0) hpy\n      simpa [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply] using hh\n    rw [hpyv0] at h\n    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.map_smul, ContinuousLinearMap.map_smul,\n      ContinuousLinearMap.map_smul] at h\n    have h' := congrArg (fun z => (⟪v0, v0⟫_ℂ)⁻¹ • z) h\n    simp only [smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hinner, one_smul] at h'\n    rw [div_eq_inv_mul]\n    exact h'\n  ext w\n  have hw : y w = y (p w) := by\n    have hh := congrArg (fun T : H →L[ℂ] H => T w) hyp\n    simpa [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply] using hh.symm\n  rw [hw, key w]\n  simp\n\nvariable {k : ℕ}\n\n/-- The image of the matrix units under a representation. -/\nnoncomputable def matrixUnit (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H))\n    (i j : Fin k) : H →L[ℂ] H := rho (Matrix.single i j 1)\n\n/-- **The commutant-producing map.**  For any operator `T`, the operator\n`Φ T = ∑ i, e i 0 * T * e 0 i` commutes with the whole matrix image. -/\nnoncomputable def matrixCommutantMap [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : H →L[ℂ] H :=\n  ∑ i : Fin k, matrixUnit rho i 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 i\n\n/-- The multiplication rule for the represented matrix units. -/\ntheorem matrixUnit_mul (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (a b i j : Fin k) :\n    matrixUnit rho a b * matrixUnit rho i j =\n      if b = i then matrixUnit rho a j else 0 := by\n  have hprod : (Matrix.single a b (1 : ℂ)) * (Matrix.single i j 1) =\n      if b = i then Matrix.single a j 1 else 0 := by\n    by_cases h : b = i\n    · subst h; rw [Matrix.single_mul_single_same]; simp\n    · simp only [h, if_false]\n      ext u v\n      simp only [Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.single, Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.zero_apply]\n      refine Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun x _ => ?_)\n      by_cases h1 : a = u ∧ b = x\n      · obtain ⟨rfl, rfl⟩ := h1\n        have hne : ¬ (i = b ∧ j = v) := fun hc => h hc.1.symm\n        simp [hne]\n      · simp [h1]\n  unfold matrixUnit\n  rw [← map_mul, hprod]\n  by_cases h : b = i <;> simp [h]\n\ntheorem matrixUnit_mul_same (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (a b c : Fin k) :\n    matrixUnit rho a b * matrixUnit rho b c = matrixUnit rho a c := by\n  rw [matrixUnit_mul]; simp\n\n/-- The represented diagonal matrix units sum to the identity operator. -/\ntheorem sum_matrixUnit_diag (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n    ∑ i : Fin k, matrixUnit rho i i = 1 := by\n  unfold matrixUnit\n  rw [← map_sum]\n  have hone : ∑ i : Fin k, Matrix.single i i (1 : ℂ) = 1 := by\n    ext a b\n    rw [Matrix.sum_apply]\n    by_cases h : a = b <;> simp [Matrix.single, Matrix.one_apply, h]\n  rw [hone, map_one]\n\n/-- Every represented matrix is a linear combination of represented matrix\nunits. -/\ntheorem rho_eq_sum_matrixUnit (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H))\n    (A : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ) :\n    rho A = ∑ a : Fin k, ∑ b : Fin k, A a b • matrixUnit rho a b := by\n  conv_lhs => rw [Matrix.matrix_eq_sum_single A]\n  rw [map_sum]\n  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun a _ => ?_)\n  rw [map_sum]\n  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun b _ => ?_)\n  unfold matrixUnit\n  rw [← map_smul]\n  congr 1\n  ext i j\n  by_cases h1 : a = i <;> by_cases h2 : b = j <;> simp [Matrix.single, h1, h2]\n\ntheorem matrixUnit_mul_commutantMap [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) (a b : Fin k) :\n    matrixUnit rho a b * matrixCommutantMap rho T =\n      matrixCommutantMap rho T * matrixUnit rho a b := by\n  unfold matrixCommutantMap\n  rw [Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_mul]\n  have hL : ∀ i : Fin k, matrixUnit rho a b * (matrixUnit rho i 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 i) =\n      if b = i then matrixUnit rho a 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 i else 0 := by\n    intro i\n    rw [← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, matrixUnit_mul rho a b i 0]\n    by_cases h : b = i <;> simp [h]\n  have hR : ∀ i : Fin k, (matrixUnit rho i 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 i) * matrixUnit rho a b =\n      if i = a then matrixUnit rho i 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 b else 0 := by\n    intro i\n    rw [mul_assoc, matrixUnit_mul rho 0 i a b]\n    by_cases h : i = a <;> simp [h]\n  simp only [hL, hR]\n  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq Finset.univ b, Finset.sum_ite_eq' Finset.univ a]\n  simp\n\ntheorem matrixCommutantMap_mem_centralizer [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    matrixCommutantMap rho T ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.range (rho : _ → H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n  rintro _ ⟨A, rfl⟩\n  rw [rho_eq_sum_matrixUnit rho A, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]\n  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun a _ => ?_)\n  rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]\n  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun b _ => ?_)\n  rw [smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, matrixUnit_mul_commutantMap rho T a b]\n\n/-- Compressing the commutant map to the `(0,0)` corner on the left. -/\ntheorem cornerProjection_mul_commutantMap [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    matrixUnit rho 0 0 * matrixCommutantMap rho T =\n      matrixUnit rho 0 0 * (T * matrixUnit rho 0 0) := by\n  unfold matrixCommutantMap\n  rw [Finset.mul_sum]\n  have h : ∀ i : Fin k, matrixUnit rho 0 0 * (matrixUnit rho i 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 i) =\n      if (0 : Fin k) = i then matrixUnit rho 0 0 * (T * matrixUnit rho 0 0) else 0 := by\n    intro i\n    rw [← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, matrixUnit_mul rho 0 0 i 0]\n    by_cases h : (0 : Fin k) = i\n    · subst h; simp [mul_assoc]\n    · simp [h]\n  simp only [h]\n  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq Finset.univ (0 : Fin k)]\n  simp\n\n/-- Compressing the commutant map to the `(0,0)` corner on the right. -/\ntheorem commutantMap_mul_cornerProjection [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    matrixCommutantMap rho T * matrixUnit rho 0 0 =\n      matrixUnit rho 0 0 * (T * matrixUnit rho 0 0) := by\n  unfold matrixCommutantMap\n  rw [Finset.sum_mul]\n  have h : ∀ i : Fin k, (matrixUnit rho i 0 * T * matrixUnit rho 0 i) * matrixUnit rho 0 0 =\n      if i = (0 : Fin k) then matrixUnit rho 0 0 * (T * matrixUnit rho 0 0) else 0 := by\n    intro i\n    rw [mul_assoc, matrixUnit_mul rho 0 i 0 0]\n    by_cases h : i = (0 : Fin k)\n    · subst h; simp [mul_assoc]\n    · simp [h]\n  simp only [h]\n  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq' Finset.univ (0 : Fin k)]\n  simp\n\n/-- **Unconditional factorhood of a represented matrix algebra.**  If a full\nmatrix algebra acts injectively (and unitally) on a Hilbert space, then every\noperator commuting both with the image and with the commutant of the image is a\nscalar.  No double commutant theorem is used. -/\ntheorem matrixRange_center_eq_scalars [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (hinj : Function.Injective rho)\n    {x : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (h1 : x ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.range (rho : _ → H →L[ℂ] H)))\n    (h2 : x ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (Set.range (rho : _ → H →L[ℂ] H)))) :\n    ∃ c : ℂ, x = c • 1 := by\n  set p : H →L[ℂ] H := matrixUnit rho 0 0 with hpdef\n  have hxe : ∀ a b : Fin k, matrixUnit rho a b * x = x * matrixUnit rho a b := fun a b =>\n    h1 _ ⟨Matrix.single a b 1, rfl⟩\n  have hp : p * p = p := matrixUnit_mul_same rho 0 0 0\n  have hp0 : p ≠ 0 := by\n    intro hcon\n    have hz : rho (Matrix.single (0 : Fin k) 0 (1 : ℂ)) = rho 0 := by rw [map_zero]; exact hcon\n    have h00 := congrFun (congrFun (hinj hz) 0) 0\n    simp [Matrix.single] at h00\n  set y : H →L[ℂ] H := p * x * p with hy0\n  have hy : y = p * y * p := by\n    rw [hy0]\n    calc p * x * p = (p * p) * x * (p * p) := by rw [hp]\n      _ = p * (p * x * p) * p := by simp only [mul_assoc]\n  have hcomm : ∀ T : H →L[ℂ] H, y * (p * T * p) = (p * T * p) * y := by\n    intro T\n    have hxphi : x * matrixCommutantMap rho T = matrixCommutantMap rho T * x :=\n      (h2 _ (matrixCommutantMap_mem_centralizer rho T)).symm\n    have hA := cornerProjection_mul_commutantMap rho T\n    have hB := commutantMap_mul_cornerProjection rho T\n    have hpp : p * (p * T * p) = p * T * p := by rw [← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, hp]\n    calc y * (p * T * p) = p * x * (p * (p * T * p)) := by\n            rw [hy0]; simp only [mul_assoc]\n      _ = p * x * (p * T * p) := by rw [hpp]\n      _ = p * x * (matrixCommutantMap rho T * p) := by rw [hB, ← hpdef]; simp only [mul_assoc]\n      _ = p * (x * matrixCommutantMap rho T) * p := by simp only [mul_assoc]\n      _ = p * (matrixCommutantMap rho T * x) * p := by rw [hxphi]\n      _ = (p * matrixCommutantMap rho T) * x * p := by simp only [mul_assoc]\n      _ = (p * (T * p)) * x * p := by rw [← hpdef] at hA; rw [hA]\n      _ = (p * T * p) * (p * x * p) := by\n            rw [show (p * T * p) * (p * x * p) = (p * T) * (p * p) * x * p by\n              simp only [mul_assoc], hp]\n            simp only [mul_assoc]\n      _ = (p * T * p) * y := by rw [hy0]\n  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := corner_commutant_eq_scalar hp hp0 hy hcomm\n  refine ⟨c, ?_⟩\n  have hpx : p * x = x * p := hxe 0 0\n  have hxp : x * p = c • p := by rw [← hc, hy0, hpx, mul_assoc, hp]\n  calc x = x * ∑ i : Fin k, matrixUnit rho i i := by rw [sum_matrixUnit_diag rho, mul_one]\n    _ = ∑ i : Fin k, x * matrixUnit rho i i := by rw [Finset.mul_sum]\n    _ = ∑ i : Fin k, c • matrixUnit rho i i := by\n        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun i _ => ?_)\n        have e1 : matrixUnit rho i 0 * (x * p) * matrixUnit rho 0 i = x * matrixUnit rho i i := by\n          have hassoc : matrixUnit rho i 0 * (x * p) * matrixUnit rho 0 i\n              = (matrixUnit rho i 0 * x) * (p * matrixUnit rho 0 i) := by simp only [mul_assoc]\n          rw [hassoc, hxe i 0, hpdef, matrixUnit_mul_same rho 0 0 i, mul_assoc,\n            matrixUnit_mul_same rho i 0 i]\n        have e2 : matrixUnit rho i 0 * (c • p) * matrixUnit rho 0 i = c • matrixUnit rho i i := by\n          rw [mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc, hpdef, matrixUnit_mul_same rho i 0 0,\n            matrixUnit_mul_same rho i 0 i]\n        rw [← e1, hxp, e2]\n    _ = c • ∑ i : Fin k, matrixUnit rho i i := by rw [Finset.smul_sum]\n    _ = c • 1 := by rw [sum_matrixUnit_diag rho]\n\n/-- The von Neumann algebra generated by an injectively represented matrix\nalgebra is a **factor**. -/\ntheorem matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter [NeZero k]\n    (rho : Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)) (hinj : Function.Injective rho) :\n    HasTrivialOperatorCenter (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated rho.range) := by\n  intro x hx hcomm\n  have hcoe : ((rho.range : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n      = Set.range (rho : _ → H →L[ℂ] H) := by\n    ext T; exact ⟨fun ⟨A, hA⟩ => ⟨A, hA⟩, fun ⟨A, hA⟩ => ⟨A, hA⟩⟩\n  have h2 : x ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (Set.range (rho : _ → H →L[ℂ] H))) := by\n    rw [← hcoe, ← StarSubalgebra.coe_vonNeumannGenerated]\n    exact hx\n  have h1 : x ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.range (rho : _ → H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n    intro m hm\n    refine hcomm m ?_\n    have hmem : m ∈ (rho.range : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n      rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, hcoe]; exact hm\n    exact StarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated _ hmem\n  exact matrixRange_center_eq_scalars rho hinj h1 h2\n\nend MatrixFactor\n\n/-! ## 6. Each finite mixed stage generates a type-I factor on the GNS space -/\n\nsection MixedStageFactor\n\n/-- The finite mixed stage as a matrix representation on the GNS space. -/\nnoncomputable def mixedMatrixRep (n : ℕ) :\n    Matrix (Fin (2 ^ n)) (Fin (2 ^ n)) ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS) :=\n  (uhfStageRep n).comp (starAlgHomOfStarAlgEquiv (qubitMatrixStarEquiv n).symm)\n\ntheorem mixedMatrixRep_injective (n : ℕ) : Function.Injective (mixedMatrixRep n) :=\n  (uhfStageRep_injective n).comp (qubitMatrixStarEquiv n).symm.injective\n\ntheorem mixedMatrixRep_range (n : ℕ) : (mixedMatrixRep n).range = mixedStage n := by\n  ext T\n  constructor\n  · rintro ⟨A, rfl⟩\n    exact ⟨(qubitMatrixStarEquiv n).symm A, rfl⟩\n  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩\n    exact ⟨qubitMatrixStarEquiv n x, by simp [mixedMatrixRep]⟩\n\n/-- **Each finite mixed stage generates a factor** (a type I_{2^n} factor) on the\nGNS Hilbert space.  Unconditional. -/\ntheorem mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter (n : ℕ) :\n    HasTrivialOperatorCenter (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated (mixedStage n)) := by\n  rw [← mixedMatrixRep_range n]\n  exact matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter _ (mixedMatrixRep_injective n)\n\nend MixedStageFactor\n\n/-! ## 7. The weak closure of the infinite mixed subsystem: conditional interface -/\n\nsection WeakClosure\n\n/-- The weak closure of the mixed C*-algebra, in the only sense available\nwithout the double commutant theorem: the von Neumann algebra it generates\n(its bicommutant). -/\nnoncomputable def mixedVonNeumann : VonNeumannAlgebra UHFGNS :=\n  StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated UHFConcreteCStar\n\ntheorem uhfRep_mem_mixedVonNeumann (z : QubitUHFAlgebra) :\n    uhfRep z ∈ (mixedVonNeumann : Set (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)) :=\n  StarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated _ (uhfRep_mem_concreteCStar z)\n\ntheorem mixedStage_le_mixedVonNeumann (n : ℕ) :\n    (mixedStage n : Set (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)) ⊆\n      (mixedVonNeumann : Set (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)) := by\n  intro T hT\n  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hT\n  exact StarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated _\n    (uhfRep_mem_concreteCStar (algebraicLimitStageStarAlgHom (f := qubitTensorPowerMap) n x))\n\n/-- **Project-local definition (normal functional).**  A functional on `B(H)`\ngiven by a single vector is normal (σ-weakly continuous); this is the only form\nof normality used here, and it is *proved*, not assumed, for the GNS vector\nstate. -/\ndef IsVectorNormal {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n    (phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) : Prop :=\n  ∃ v : H, ∀ x : H →L[ℂ] H, phi x = ⟪v, x v⟫_ℂ\n\n/-- The GNS vector functional of the mixed reference representation. -/\nnoncomputable def uhfVectorState : (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ where\n  toFun x := ⟪uhfCyclicVector, x uhfCyclicVector⟫_ℂ\n  map_add' x y := by simp [inner_add_right]\n  map_smul' c x := by simp [inner_smul_right]\n\n@[simp] theorem uhfVectorState_apply (x : UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS) :\n    uhfVectorState x = ⟪uhfCyclicVector, x uhfCyclicVector⟫_ℂ := rfl\n\ntheorem uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal : IsVectorNormal uhfVectorState :=\n  ⟨uhfCyclicVector, fun _ => rfl⟩\n\ntheorem uhfVectorState_one : uhfVectorState 1 = 1 := by\n  show ⟪uhfCyclicVector, (1 : UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS) uhfCyclicVector⟫_ℂ = 1\n  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, uhfCyclicVector_norm]\n  norm_num\n\ntheorem uhfVectorState_positive (x : UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS) :\n    ∃ r : ℝ, 0 ≤ r ∧ uhfVectorState (star x * x) = (r : ℂ) := by\n  refine ⟨‖x uhfCyclicVector‖ ^ 2, by positivity, ?_⟩\n  show ⟪uhfCyclicVector, (star x * x) uhfCyclicVector⟫_ℂ = _\n  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint,\n    ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n  norm_num\n\n/-- The GNS vector state restricts to the canonical normalized trace on the\nrepresented algebraic mixed subsystem. -/\ntheorem uhfVectorState_uhfRep (z : QubitUHFAlgebra) :\n    uhfVectorState (uhfRep z) = qubitUHFTrace z :=\n  uhfRep_vector_state z\n\n/-- **Auxiliary assumptions (explicitly named).**  The three analytic facts about\nthe weak closure of the mixed algebra which are *not* proved in this package.\nThey are exactly the statements whose proofs require weak/strong-operator limit\narguments (Kaplansky density and the double commutant theorem) or the\nextremality of the UHF trace. -/\nstructure MixedWeakClosurePremises : Prop where\n  /-- the GNS vector state is tracial on the whole weak closure -/\n  tracial : ∀ x ∈ (mixedVonNeumann : Set (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)),\n    ∀ y ∈ (mixedVonNeumann : Set (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)),\n      uhfVectorState (x * y) = uhfVectorState (y * x)\n  /-- the GNS vector state is faithful on the weak closure -/\n  faithful : ∀ x ∈ (mixedVonNeumann : Set (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)),\n    uhfVectorState (star x * x) = 0 → x = 0\n  /-- the weak closure is a factor -/\n  factor : HasTrivialOperatorCenter mixedVonNeumann\n\n/-- **Project-local definition (hyperfinite finite-factor model).**  The list of\nfeatures that the manuscript's phrase \"hyperfinite type II₁ factor\" is taken to\nabbreviate here.  This is *not* the Murray–von Neumann/Connes uniqueness\ntheorem: no claim is made that a von Neumann algebra with these features is\nisomorphic to *the* hyperfinite II₁ factor. -/\nstructure IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel\n    {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n    (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : Prop where\n  /-- trivial centre -/\n  factor : HasTrivialOperatorCenter M\n  /-- a normal, unital, positive, tracial, faithful state on `M` -/\n  finite_trace : ∃ phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ,\n    IsVectorNormal phi ∧ phi 1 = 1 ∧\n    (∀ x : H →L[ℂ] H, ∃ r : ℝ, 0 ≤ r ∧ phi (star x * x) = (r : ℂ)) ∧\n    (∀ x ∈ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), ∀ y ∈ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)),\n      phi (x * y) = phi (y * x)) ∧\n    (∀ x ∈ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), phi (star x * x) = 0 → x = 0)\n  /-- an increasing chain of finite matrix subalgebras with dense union in a\n  C*-subalgebra generating `M` -/\n  hyperfinite : ∃ S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H),\n    Nonempty (IsMatricialChain S) ∧ StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated S = M\n  /-- matrix subalgebras of unbounded size sit inside `M`: `M` is not of finite\n  type I -/\n  infinite : ∀ N : ℕ, ∃ (k : ℕ) (S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)),\n    N ≤ k ∧ (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ⊆ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∧\n      Nonempty ((S) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ)\n\n/-- **Conditional classification of the infinite mixed subsystem.**  Under the\nthree explicitly named premises, the weak closure of the infinite mixed\nsubsystem is a factor with a normal faithful tracial state, hyperfinite in the\nmatricial-chain sense, and contains matrix subalgebras of unbounded size. -/\ntheorem mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor (h : MixedWeakClosurePremises) :\n    IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel mixedVonNeumann where\n  factor := h.factor\n  finite_trace :=\n    ⟨uhfVectorState, uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal, uhfVectorState_one,\n      uhfVectorState_positive, h.tracial, h.faithful⟩\n  hyperfinite := ⟨UHFConcreteCStar, ⟨uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain⟩, rfl⟩\n  infinite N := by\n    refine ⟨2 ^ N, mixedStage N, Nat.le_of_lt Nat.lt_two_pow_self,\n      mixedStage_le_mixedVonNeumann N, ⟨mixedStage_matrixEquiv N⟩⟩\n\nend WeakClosure\n\nend StabilizerHyperfinite\n--- P49B CLOSEOUT ---\n# P49B closeout review - analytic von Neumann bicommutant theorem\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256 `6973bbc16ab59440f27f6b45b722ca8c482dbc7d35e724386cdd1d15cd550b96`)\nand extracted without a build, update, or dependency fetch at\n`aristotle_responses/P49B-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49b-sn5_fvfw_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` was integrated.  Its\nSHA-256 is `7f6101e5c55273dfc4a48661b0d4852183ac3e015a844764a7075e542f0fc3ce`\nin both quarantine and the live project.  The archive and extraction remain\nignored raw response records.  No manuscript file was changed.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `H` with `[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]`\nand `A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H ->L[ℂ] H)`, the module defines\n`VonNeumannBicommutant.strongClosure` using Mathlib's\n`PointwiseConvergenceCLM`/`StrongOperator.SOT` topology.  Its central theorem\ndeclarations are:\n\n- `VonNeumannBicommutant.mem_strongClosure_iff`, the exact arbitrary-finite-set\n  strong-neighbourhood criterion;\n- `VonNeumannBicommutant.exists_mem_approx_on_fin`, simultaneous approximation\n  of every element of the bicommutant on a finite family of vectors;\n- `VonNeumannBicommutant.bicommutant_subset_strongClosure` and\n  `VonNeumannBicommutant.strongClosure_subset_bicommutant`;\n- `VonNeumannBicommutant.strongClosure_eq_bicommutant`, namely\n  `strongClosure (A : Set (H ->L[ℂ] H)) = Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer A)`;\n- `VonNeumannBicommutant.strongClosure_eq_vonNeumannGenerated` and\n  `VonNeumannBicommutant.strongClosure_eq_self_iff`.\n\nCompleteness is the only additional analytic premise beyond a complex inner\nproduct space: it supplies the orthogonal projection onto the closed cyclic\nsubspace.  `StarSubalgebra` supplies the required unit, used to put the\namplified cyclic vector in that subspace.  No nondegeneracy hypothesis,\nstructure-field replacement, external theorem token, or user axiom is used.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The live Lean project proves both inclusions and the equality by finite amplification.  `ampOp`, `ampIn`, the matrix-entry commutant calculation, invariant-subspace projection commutation, and finite-family cyclic approximation are all local declarations in the integrated module. |\n| partial | None within the stated P49B gate.  The theorem is abstract infrastructure, not a proof that any project-specific compressed quasi-local algebra satisfies a density hypothesis. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the stated gate.  P49C remains required for bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density, and P50 remains required for the corner trace/normality passage. |\n| failed | None.  No compilation, axiom, placeholder, provenance, or scope failure was found. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met: the result is about arbitrary finite\nstrong neighbourhoods and nets, not a sequential-closure substitute.  The\nhard inclusion uses the usual diagonal finite amplification/cyclic-subspace\nargument; the reverse inclusion uses P49A strong closedness of the commutant.\n\n## Manuscript boundary\n\nThe packet declares source basis `main.tex:1269-1287`.  Those lines identify\nthe intended later use: extending from the compressed C-star algebra to the\nvon Neumann corner and requiring strong density before the Kaplansky step.\nP49B is explicitly labelled **Lean infrastructure only** and makes no claim\nthat this manuscript density statement, the existence of its uniformly bounded\nnet, or its compressed-corner consequence has been formalized.  It provides\nonly the independently proved double-commutant tool.  In particular it does\nnot represent the Kaplansky assertion at `main.tex:1275-1281`; that remains\nP49C work.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49B, lane `shared` - correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P49A is integrated and locally audited; its live source is\n  byte-identical to the corresponding quarantine predecessor.  The imported\n  algebraic bicommutant core is local support, not a later package.  No P49C,\n  P50, or later package is imported.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: for a unital complex star subalgebra\n  of bounded operators, the bicommutant equals its strong-operator closure.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module contains no\n  Kaplansky unit-ball density, corner trace, normality/faithfulness,\n  finiteness/fullness, global trace/weight, central type-III exclusion, or\n  factor-classification theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake env lean aristotle_responses/P49B-quarantine/.../VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` - passed from the live built project; no build/update/fetch was run in quarantine.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem` - passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem Formalization` - passed.\n- `lake build` - passed in the live project.\n- `#print axioms` for `strongClosure_eq_bicommutant`,\n  `strongClosure_eq_vonNeumannGenerated`, `mem_strongClosure_iff`,\n  `exists_mem_approx_on_fin`, and `strongClosure_eq_self_iff` - each reports\n  only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan - no executable `sorry`, `admit`,\n  user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide`;\n  matches are only negative-scope documentation.\n- Quarantine/live byte comparison, SHA-256 comparison, and `git diff --check` - passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that `strongClosure` is\ntopological SOT closure rather than norm closure; the finite-neighbourhood\ncriterion works in both directions; the `n = 0` amplification case is covered\nwithout an empty-family exception; and the cyclic-subspace step uses unitality,\nstar invariance, and completeness precisely where needed.  The remaining risk\nis deliberately outside P49B: this theorem does not supply Kaplansky bounded\ndensity, nor does compilation establish any project-specific normal trace or\nvon Neumann-algebra conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P49B candidate, its closeout review, and\nthe ignored raw archive/quarantine snapshot.  Preserved unchanged: the\npre-existing untracked P49A candidate and P49/P49A reviews.  No commit, push,\nmanuscript modification, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch\nwas performed.\n--- P49A CLOSEOUT ---\n# P49A closeout review — strong-operator closed concrete von Neumann algebras\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256 `eb1bd6ddf17213aaf2ba0062f0fe7ba5b0851f4a46eff6ea655801bb3f70d56e`)\nand extracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P49A-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49a-p0kpdbli_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` was integrated\ninto the live project. Its SHA-256 is\n`dfb39289d895c16400e05145112320a42e6d1b61736859edbba153d02df0571a`\nin both the quarantine snapshot and live project. The archive and extraction\nremain raw response records. No manuscript file was modified.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `H` with `[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]`, the module\ndefines the SOT synonym `StrongOperator.SOT H`, the pointwise predicate\n`StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto`, and `StrongOperator.IsStronglyClosed`.\nThe exact core theorems are:\n\n- `StrongOperator.stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot` and\n  `StrongOperator.tendsto_sot_iff_forall_tendsto`;\n- `StrongOperator.mem_centralizer_of_stronglyTendsto` and\n  `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_centralizer`;\n- under `[CompleteSpace H]`,\n  `StrongOperator.coe_vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_centralizer`,\n  `StrongOperator.mem_vonNeumannAlgebra_of_stronglyTendsto`, and\n  `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra`;\n- `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.const_mul`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_const`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_bounded`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_norm_le`, and\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.compress`.\n\nThe only analytic assumptions are the standard complex inner-product-space\nstructure, and completeness precisely where Mathlib's concrete\n`VonNeumannAlgebra H` requires it. The joint-product theorem explicitly\nrequires a uniform norm bound on its left family. No analytic conclusion is a\nstructure field or axiom.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | All four packet conclusions are proved: SOT/net equivalence; strong closedness of arbitrary commutants; strong closedness of concrete von Neumann algebras using `M = M''`; and fixed-side plus uniformly bounded joint product stability. |\n| partial | None within the stated P49A infrastructure target. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the stated gate. The analytic double-commutant theorem and Kaplansky density remain separate P49B/P49C work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe mathematical target is met at its stated scope. In particular,\n`isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra` is a closure theorem for an already\ngiven Mathlib concrete von Neumann algebra; it does not identify the strong\nclosure of an arbitrary star subalgebra with its bicommutant.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49A, Lane shared.\n- **Predecessors:** P48 was previously integrated and locally audited. The\n  candidate imports only the locally present supporting module\n  `AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`; it imports no P49B, P49C,\n  P50, or later package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: commutants and therefore Mathlib concrete\n  von Neumann algebras are closed under strong-operator limits.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. No double-commutant equality\n  with a strong closure, Kaplansky density, corner trace, faithfulness,\n  finiteness, fullness, or type classification is asserted.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for all four core\n  conclusions and the compression corollary — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate — no executable\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration. Search hits occur only\n  in the file's explicit negative-scope documentation.\n- Quarantine/live byte comparison, SHA-256 comparison, and `git diff --check`\n  — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that the centralizer proof\npasses the commutation equation pointwise through the two strong limits; that\nthe concrete von Neumann result uses only its defining bicommutant equality;\nand that the product proof has the required uniform norm bound on the left\nfactor. The remaining risk is exactly the deliberately deferred P49B/P49C\nanalytic identification and density work; compilation and axiom inspection do\nnot establish those results.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P49A candidate, its ignored quarantine\narchive and extraction, and this closeout review. No commit, push, manuscript\nchange, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed\nlocally. The new candidate and review are the only working-tree changes from\nthis closeout.\n--- DIRECT IMPORT HASH COMPARISON ---\n52239a0484cab088978d3ababbe640a365409730cc415edac53b49aca05db803  Formalization/DyadicTensorTower.lean\n52239a0484cab088978d3ababbe640a365409730cc415edac53b49aca05db803  aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/Formalization/DyadicTensorTower.lean\n786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9  AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean\n786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9  aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean\nf15997d639f13dcaea7a708a9813e0579eb5749ba894a74d199806cf2274de35  AristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean\nf15997d639f13dcaea7a708a9813e0579eb5749ba894a74d199806cf2274de35  aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean\n--- SOURCE CONTRACT LOCATOR ---\n13-\n14-| Source locator | What the manuscript says | Formalization status |\n15-| --- | --- | --- |\n16-| `main.tex:1671-1679` | Defines short-range order through a local symplectic basis, with `W_Gamma = span{z_i : i in P}` and finite support. | Requires a precise Lean model of the infinite Pauli/symplectic data. |\n17:| `main.tex:1740-1752` | States the short-range regional-algebra theorem, with an asserted factorization `A_Gamma` into a pure-sector type-I factor and a core factor that is finite type I or hyperfinite `II_1`. | Target statement; not established by current Lean artifacts. |\n18-| `main.tex:1915-1920` | Proposes an adapted symplectic basis and a star-isomorphism from an infinite Pauli algebra to `A_Gamma`. | External assumption/gap until the source construction is formalized. |\n19:| `main.tex:1927-1931` | Writes a pure/mixed product density state. | Finite density-matrix fragments are formalized; the infinite model is not. |\n20:| `main.tex:1945-1967` | Proposes the GNS/tensor-factor and type conclusions. | Conditional GNS transport is formalized; analytic product and type conclusions are not. |\n21-| `main.tex:1970-2004` | Proposes quasi-equivalence and normal-folium transport. | Not formalized. |\n22-\n23-The wording above is a locator-oriented paraphrase, not a replacement for the\n24-manuscript.\n--\n34-3. the product-state formula and hypotheses making the GNS representation a\n35-   spatial tensor product;\n36-4. the von Neumann closure, normality, and quasi-equivalence assumptions needed\n37-   to transport the claimed factor type; and\n38:5. any hyperfiniteness or trace theorem used for the core factor.\n39-\n40-None of these assumptions is supplied merely by the phrase “short-range\n41-order” in the current manuscript source.\n42-\n--\n47-- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is finite-dimensional, a normalized tracial\n48-  state can be obtained from the finite matrix trace together with the core\n49-  trace;\n50-- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is infinite-dimensional, the appropriate\n51:  conclusion is a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight on the `II_infinity`\n52-  target, not a tracial state.\n53-\n54-This is a correction to the intended theorem contract, not a claim that the\n55-current manuscript already states or proves the corrected dichotomy.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
