{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- MANUSCRIPT LOCATOR ---'\nnl -ba sources/manuscript/main.tex | sed -n '1945,1967p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- LOAD-BEARING DECLARATIONS ---'\nrg -n '\"'^(def|structure|noncomputable def|theorem) (qubitMatrixStarEquiv|qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace|qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor|qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter|qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra|uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain|matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter|mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter|mixedVonNeumann|MixedWeakClosurePremises|IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel|mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor)'\"' AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- FINAL STATUS ---'\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"--- MANUSCRIPT LOCATOR ---\n  1945\t    on $\\G$ can be represented by a density matrix which is a tensor product of\n  1946\t    pure states or maximally mixed states. We can then form the GNS\n  1947\t    Hilbert space $\\cH_{\\tilde{\\w}}$ with representation $\\pi_{\\tilde{\\w}}$ of $\\cP_I$, which is an infinite tensor\n  1948\t    product that we can decompose into a tensor product \n  1949\t    \\begin{equation}\n  1950\t        \\cH_{\\tilde{\\w}} = \\cK \\otimes \\cK',\n  1951\t    \\end{equation}\n  1952\t    where $\\cK$ is an (infinite) tensor product with vacuum $\\ket{0}$ and\n  1953\t    $\\cK'$ is the GNS representation associated to the maximally mixed state.\n  1954\t    We can thus use the type classification of Araki-Woods factors on\n  1955\t    \\begin{equation}\n  1956\t        \\pi_{\\tilde{\\w}}(\\cP_I)'' = \\cB(\\cK) \\bar{\\otimes} \\cR,\n  1957\t    \\end{equation}\n  1958\t    which follows from \\LS{CITE TENSOR PRODUCT THM WE PROVED}. Here, the exact\n  1959\t    types depend on whether we have finitely or infinitely many maximally\n  1960\t    entangled or pure factors in the state $\\tilde{\\w}$. If there are\n  1961\t    infinitely many pure pieces $\\ket{0}$, then $\\cB(\\cK)$ is a type I$_\\infty$ factor,\n  1962\t    otherwise it is type I$_n$ with $n$ being the number of factors in the\n  1963\t    state $\\ket{0}$.\n  1964\t    This coincides with the dimension of $W_\\G$. If we have infinitely many\n  1965\t    maximally entangled pieces, then $\\cR$ is the hyperfinite type II$_1$\n  1966\t    factor, otherwise its again a finite matrix algebra of type I$_k$. This\n  1967\t    fixes the possible types of $\\pi_{\\tilde{\\w}}(\\cP_I)$. \n--- LOAD-BEARING DECLARATIONS ---\n197:noncomputable def qubitMatrixStarEquiv : (n : ℕ) →\n205:theorem qubitMatrixStarEquiv_succ_apply (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower (n + 1))\n213:theorem qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower n) :\n291:noncomputable def qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor (n : ℕ) :\n314:theorem qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter : HasScalarCenter QubitUHFAlgebra := by\n331:theorem qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra (k : ℕ) :\n410:noncomputable def uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain : IsMatricialChain UHFConcreteCStar where\n683:theorem matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter [NeZero k]\n725:theorem mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter (n : ℕ) :\n739:noncomputable def mixedVonNeumann : VonNeumannAlgebra UHFGNS :=\n798:structure MixedWeakClosurePremises : Prop where\n814:structure IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel\n840:theorem mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor (h : MixedWeakClosurePremises) :\n--- FINAL STATUS ---\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n","exit_code":0,"